  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best config so far is config_041 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) at 0.7250 acc. We've confirmed that scgpt is a poor RNA encoder (0.5200 in config_015) and that imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted is the strongest image/aggregation/fusion stack. However, pca_n2000 — the third and only remaining RNA encoder — has never been tested in any multimodal setting. This experiment tests whether pca_n2000 (a linear dimensionality-reduction encoder) can match or approach scvi_n200 in the best-known architecture, or whether scvi_n200's learned latent space is essential. Clarifying this is important because if pca_n2000 is competitive, it offers a cheaper RNA pathway and opens the remaining 3 experiments to fine-tuning around it; if it underperforms significantly, we can confidently lock in scvi_n200 and spend remaining budget on marginal refinements (e.g., singleprofile variant config_049). Expected relative cost: moderate — PCA encoding is cheaper than scvi_n200, but imagenet_vit_l and transformer aggregation keep total cost comparable to config_041 (~3–4 GPU hours), so this is not a high-cost gamble for an untested dimension."
}

